      "lines": [
        "Both bundlers are installed: vite and webpack, @nextcloud/webpack-vue-config.",
        "  The build scripts decide which one produces the committed assets; the other keeps its config, its plugins and its share of every install, and drifts out of use without anyone noticing."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "runtime-dirs-not-shipped",
      "lines": [
        "context/ is read at run time and is not in the shipped file set: lib/Service/SignatureService.php:1176 reaches it through __DIR__.",
        "  A release ships only the paths of the keep set (the ncmake core and ncmake.mk), so the tarball lacks it and the app fails in the code that reads it, while the build and the packing pass. In ncmake.mk, keep_extra += context ships it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence agpl (appinfo/info.xml, package.json), AGPL-3.0-or-later (composer.json), LICENSES/ holds AGPL-3.0-or-later.txt, Apache-2.0.txt, CC0-1.0.txt, GPL-3.0-or-later.txt, LicenseRef-NextcloudTrademarks.txt, MIT.txt.",
        "  agpl in appinfo/info.xml is a deprecated App Store value, shown there as AGPLv3+, which is AGPL-3.0-or-later. With min-version 35 info.xml can state an SPDX id instead.",
        "  No SPDX id: agpl (package.json). Only an SPDX id says which licence is meant, and for a GNU licence whether -only or -or-later."
      ]
    },
